 "submission": {
  "summary": "F-14's oil rate after its last regime change in early 2012 is essentially flat, so the fit suggests a 12-month forecast from 2013-01-02 of about 321725 Sm3 (P50) with a range of 289444 Sm3 (P90) to 344792 Sm3 (P10), but confidence is low because the fit suggests a very poor fit (r2_log 0.01139) and almost no decline (0.07073 per year), most likely because the window spans a plateau rather than a clear decline.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "The correct window for forecasting starts after the last oil-rate regime change on 2012-02-05, when weekly mean oil rate fell from 2,082 to 1,142 Sm3/d with a shift of -45.13% and has since stayed near the lower level through 2012-12 (water cut 0.6381 to 0.7564, oil rate 1,017 to 1,335 Sm3/d per producing day).",
