   {
    "claim": "Confidence is low: the plateau-like behaviour makes the harmonic fit statistically indistinguishable from exponential (AIC -959.97 vs -959.94) and the about 10% difference between P90 and P50 (55,348 Sm3 spread) understates operational risk from frequent field-wide shut-ins of up to 32 days recorded after 2010. For comparison, a longer exponential fit on 2010-01-24 to 2013-01-01 has good statistics (r2_log 0.7747, di 0.3453 per year) and would forecast 258598 Sm3 P50, but it violates the regime-change rule by averaging across the February 2012 drop and therefore overstates decline.",
